WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.833 --> 00:00:04.083
(powerful dance music)

00:00:05.297 --> 00:00:09.047
- What I feel when I am
dancing, I feel free.

00:00:09.969 --> 00:00:12.201
I just feel confident, I feel strong,

00:00:12.201 --> 00:00:14.701
I feel in control of who I am.

00:00:16.097 --> 00:00:18.008
I knew this is what I wanted to do.

00:00:18.008 --> 00:00:20.736
I didn't wanna do anything else but this.

00:00:20.736 --> 00:00:21.653
It's crazy.

00:00:27.459 --> 00:00:29.734
My name is Akira
Armstrong, and I am the CEO

00:00:29.734 --> 00:00:31.657
and founder of Pretty Big Movement,

00:00:31.657 --> 00:00:32.692
which is a full-figured,

00:00:32.692 --> 00:00:34.942
professional dance company.

00:00:35.858 --> 00:00:37.972
I started Pretty Big
Movement nine years ago,

00:00:37.972 --> 00:00:39.560
and I felt that there was a void

00:00:39.560 --> 00:00:41.067
in main-stream media,

00:00:41.067 --> 00:00:42.610
where it wasn't a platform for plus-size,

00:00:42.610 --> 00:00:44.360
professional dancers.

00:00:45.374 --> 00:00:46.673
I didn't fit in.

00:00:46.673 --> 00:00:48.376
Even when walkin' into auditions,

00:00:48.376 --> 00:00:51.254
I didn't feel like I belong.

00:00:51.254 --> 00:00:54.060
The typical expected body type is

00:00:54.060 --> 00:00:56.009
the ballerinas, you know, the long legs,

00:00:56.009 --> 00:00:58.895
the long arms, long torso.

00:00:58.895 --> 00:01:01.054
It's upsetting that society

00:01:01.054 --> 00:01:04.343
puts this label on dancers because for me,

00:01:04.343 --> 00:01:06.176
it's about the talent.

00:01:07.887 --> 00:01:11.304
I had booked this major gig with Beyoncé,

00:01:12.287 --> 00:01:14.525
I decided, "Well, lemme audition

00:01:14.525 --> 00:01:16.393
"for more representation."

00:01:16.393 --> 00:01:17.737
I auditioned for at least

00:01:17.737 --> 00:01:19.645
five different agencies, and they all kept

00:01:19.645 --> 00:01:20.620
sayin' the same thing:

00:01:20.620 --> 00:01:23.099
"She's good but we don't
know how to market her."

00:01:23.099 --> 00:01:25.985
And I got tired of hearin' that.

00:01:25.985 --> 00:01:29.020
Even though I struggle with things,

00:01:29.020 --> 00:01:30.539
it was my passion.

00:01:30.539 --> 00:01:31.711
It's somethin' that I wanted to do;

00:01:31.711 --> 00:01:33.623
it's somethin' that I love.

00:01:33.623 --> 00:01:37.358
And I kept pushing, kept
pushing, kept pushing.

00:01:37.358 --> 00:01:38.903
And it just got to a
point where I was like,

00:01:38.903 --> 00:01:41.908
“This is really what I wanna do."

00:01:41.908 --> 00:01:44.021
We came up with the name Pretty Big

00:01:44.021 --> 00:01:47.879
and from there I said,
"I need a pack a girls,

00:01:47.879 --> 00:01:51.047
"who know how to move,
who know how to dance."

00:01:51.047 --> 00:01:54.099
We have a range of young ladies

00:01:54.099 --> 00:01:56.825
who are professional dancers,

00:01:56.825 --> 00:01:58.779
they work hard to prove themselves,

00:01:58.779 --> 00:02:01.535
not only to me but also to themselves.

00:02:01.535 --> 00:02:04.299
Five, six, seven, here we go, and a one,

00:02:04.299 --> 00:02:06.736
and a two, and a three, jump!

00:02:06.736 --> 00:02:08.526
One thing is that we do,

00:02:08.526 --> 00:02:10.477
is our Pretty Big Movement workshop.

00:02:10.477 --> 00:02:12.869
Anybody is welcome to
come to our workshops.

00:02:12.869 --> 00:02:16.278
I am pretty big, and I am powerful because

00:02:16.278 --> 00:02:18.307
I feel nothin' but love in this room.

00:02:18.307 --> 00:02:21.067
We do power circles and that portion

00:02:21.067 --> 00:02:23.135
of the workshop becomes very emotional.

00:02:23.135 --> 00:02:24.880
- Each and every day I'm
learning to love myself,

00:02:24.880 --> 00:02:28.819
and those who tear me
down, can't keep me down.

00:02:28.819 --> 00:02:30.648
- We've had people say,
"I've beat divorce,

00:02:30.648 --> 00:02:33.308
"I've beat suicide; I was a rape victim."

00:02:33.308 --> 00:02:35.825
- I beat cancer, so I
wasn't gonna let this foot,

00:02:35.825 --> 00:02:37.115
keep me back!
- They just feel

00:02:37.115 --> 00:02:39.904
comfortable enough to
just spill it all out.

00:02:39.904 --> 00:02:41.932
The misconceptions that people have

00:02:41.932 --> 00:02:43.278
about plus-sized women,

00:02:43.278 --> 00:02:45.596
"We are lazy, we have low self-esteem."

00:02:45.596 --> 00:02:47.897
We are built! (loud cheers)

00:02:47.897 --> 00:02:49.533
"We don't care about our appearance,

00:02:49.533 --> 00:02:51.038
"we are non-existent."

00:02:51.038 --> 00:02:52.079
And we exist.

00:02:52.079 --> 00:02:53.337
This is who I am!

00:02:53.337 --> 00:02:57.504
Plus-size and fabulous! (giggles)

